      "desktop": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"100%\" style=\"height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 650\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"amazon-incrementality-en-d-title amazon-incrementality-en-d-desc\" xml:lang=\"en\" data-kind=\"incrementality\" data-variant=\"desktop\">\n<title id=\"amazon-incrementality-en-d-title\">Attributed sales and additional sales</title>\n<desc id=\"amazon-incrementality-en-d-desc\">Fictional l0g model M02. The same traffic: 100 clicks at $1.20, costing $120. Ten attributed orders of $50 produce $500 of attributed revenue and a rounded ROAS of 4.17. Chosen assumption, not an Amazon estimate: 60 percent of the orders are additional, or six; four would have happened without the campaign. Contribution before advertising is $15 per order. Attribution view: 10 times 15 minus 120 equals plus $30. Incremental view: 6 times 15 minus 120 equals minus $30. Incremental break-even CPC: 0.10 times 0.60 times 15 equals $0.90. The inputs are illustrative assumptions. Sources M02, S08, S09 and S15; the methodological literature is not an Amazon study.</desc>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1000\" height=\"650\" fill=\"var(--color-surface)\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"10.400000000000002\" width=\"984\" height=\"39.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"none\" rx=\"0\" id=\"amazon-incrementality-en-d-region-1\" data-label-region=\"true\"/>\n<text x=\"32\" y=\"38\" fill=\"var(--color-amber)\" font-family=\"l0g Amazon Auctions\" font-size=\"23\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" data-panel=\"amazon-incrementality-en-d-region-1\">ILLUSTRATIVE MODEL · M02</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"47.0\" width=\"984\" height=\"51.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"none\" rx=\"0\" id=\"amazon-incrementality-en-d-region-2\" data-label-region=\"true\"/>\n<text x=\"32\" y=\"83\" fill=\"var(--color-paper)\" font-family=\"l0g Amazon Auctions\" font-size=\"30\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" data-panel=\"amazon-incrementality-en-d-region-2\">100 clicks · $120 spent</text>\n<