    "revenue": {
      "desktop": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"100%\" style=\"height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 690\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"amazon-revenue-en-d-title amazon-revenue-en-d-desc\" xml:lang=\"en\" data-kind=\"revenue\" data-variant=\"desktop\">\n<title id=\"amazon-revenue-en-d-title\">Amazon advertising revenue</title>\n<desc id=\"amazon-revenue-en-d-desc\">Amazon worldwide Advertising services revenue, all formats within the line item, current US dollars, US GAAP. Full calendar years in millions of dollars: 2021, 31,160; 2022, 37,739; 2023, 46,906; 2024, 56,214; 2025, 68,635. The annual chart starts at zero; billion-dollar labels are rounded to one decimal. A separate quarterly panel shows Q3 2025, $17,703 million, and Q3 2026, $19,637 million. Reported nominal growth is 11 percent. Prime Day moved to the second quarter in most major countries in 2026. No mathematical adjustment of these revenues and no annualisation of 2026. These revenues measure neither CPC, reserve-related overcharges nor Ads profit. Sources S13 and S12 for annual figures; S10 and S11 for the quarter.</desc>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1000\" height=\"690\" fill=\"var(--color-surface)\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"10.400000000000002\" width=\"984\" height=\"39.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"none\" rx=\"0\" id=\"amazon-revenue-en-d-region-1\" data-label-region=\"true\"/>\n<text x=\"32\" y=\"38\" fill=\"var(--color-signal)\" font-family=\"l0g Amazon Auctions\" font-size=\"23\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" data-panel=\"amazon-revenue-en-d-region-1\">WORLDWIDE REVENUE · US GAAP</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"52.8\" width=\"984\" height=\"44.199999999999996\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"none\" rx=\"0\" id=\"amazon-revenue-en-d-region-2\" data-label-region=\"true\"/>\n<text x=\"32\" y=\"84\" fill=\"var(--color-muted)\" font-family=\"l0g Amazon Auctions\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" data-panel=\"amazon-revenue-en-d-region-2\">Advertising services · cu